abstract: "TFT (Truncation Framework of Trust) is an original academic framework that reconceptualizes trust as a cognitive economic behavior: trust is truncation — under attention scarcity constraints, agents stop monitoring at some point and fill the unmonitored gap with trust extrapolation."
keywords:
  - "trust"
  - "attention scarcity"
  - "bounded rationality"
  - "contract theory"
  - "coordinate system"
  - "trust truncation"
  - "AI industry"
  - "RLHF"
  - "AI alignment"
